# The Long Table. Homely, attentive, a little too interested in you. Nothing is ever described.
# No regard, no threats; the family's memory stays its three words (guest, family, crossed).

conv table.road.host
for table:road
topic "Ask about the road ahead."
prio world
voice table

node start
  say "Clear to the bridge, if you keep off the verges. The trucks went through this morning, both of them."
  say "Where are you headed? Is anyone expecting you?"
  > @alone "Nobody. I'm on my own." -> alone
  > @expected "They're expecting me back by dark." -> expected
  > @road "Just passing." -> passing

node alone
  say "Then you'll eat with us. Mother cooks for twenty and there are never twenty. Supper's at half six."
  do claim:alone
  > @maybe "Maybe I will." -> hub
  > @no "Another time." -> hub

node expected
  say "Then you'd best be on your way before the light goes. People worry. Come another day, with them."
  do claim:expected
  > @thanks "Thanks for the road." -> hub

node passing
  say "Everyone is. That's what roads are for. The offer stands, whenever you're passing next."
  > @back1 "I'll remember." -> hub

conv table.mother.house
for table:mother
when !table:crossed
topic "Ask about the farm."
prio flavour
voice table

node start
  say "It was my husband's people's. Always a big house, always a long table. Sit, sit. You're thin."
  say "Have you been bitten, love? We ask everyone. You can tell me."
  > @no "No. Not bitten." -> fine
  > @bite "I've a bite. Here." -> bitten   if bite_shown
  > @boy "Is the boy yours?" -> boy

node fine
  say "Good. Then there's no hurry at all, is there. Stay as long as you like."
  > @back1 "Something else." -> hub

node bitten
  say "Oh, love. Then you'll eat first, and we'll say a kind word over you, and you'll go before dark."
  do call:slot:2
  > @back2 "Something else." -> hub

node boy
  say "He came with the others. He's ours now. He eats what he's given."
  > @back3 "Something else." -> hub
